/-!
# Restriction to a divisor and the different in *Flips and abundance*

The definitions of FA 16.3.3, 16.3.6, 16.5 and 16.6 leading to the different: the dualizing
sheaf `ω_X = H^{-d}(π^! k)`, the restriction `f|_S` of rational functions regular along a reduced
closed subscheme `i : S → X`, the saturated restriction `i^{[*]}𝓕`, the embedded dualizing sheaf
`Ω_S ⊆ K(S)`, the restrictions `i^w_C`, `i^w : WSh_S(X) → WSh(S)_ℚ` and `i^w` on
`WSh_S(X)_ℚ`, the differents `𝒟iff_S(0)`, `𝒟iff_S(B)` of FA 16.5, and the different
`Diff_S(B) ∈ WDiv(S)_ℚ` of FA 16.6.

## Setting

`i : S ⟶ X` is a closed immersion of schemes, playing the role of the reduced closed subscheme
`S ⊆ X` of pure codimension one of FA 16.3.6; the closed subset `S ⊆ X` is `closedRange i`. As in
`MMP.Foundations.Flips.WeilSubsheaf`, the codimension of a point is its coheight in the
specialization order; a point `P` of `S` has codimension `≤ 1` in `S` if
`Order.coheight P ≤ 1` in the scheme `S`. The generic points `ξ` of the irreducible components of
`S` are the images `i(η_Z)` of the generic points `η_Z` of the irreducible components `Z` of the
scheme `S` (`maximal_closure_image_genericPoint` shows these are the generic points of the
irreducible components of the closed subset `closedRange i` used by `HasGoodSupport`).

## The group `WSh(S)_ℚ`

The book writes `WSh(S)_ℚ` multiplicatively; here it is written additively. The group law
`(1/n)𝓛 + (1/m)𝓛' = (1/nm)(𝓛^[m] · 𝓛'^[n])` is not available on `QWeilDivisorialSheaf` (the
product of two Weil divisorial subsheaves is only known to be an `𝒪`-submodule of `K`), so an
identity `c₁ + c₂ = c₃` is stated on representatives by `QWeilDivisorialSheaf.IsSum`: for some
representatives `cᵢ = (1/nᵢ)𝓛ᵢ`, the pair `(𝓛₁^[n₂] · 𝓛₂^[n₁], n₁n₂)` is equivalent to `(𝓛₃, n₃)`
in the sense of FA 16.1.3. Likewise `(1/m)·(1/n)𝓝 = (1/mn)𝓝` is written on representatives.

## The dualizing sheaf

`IsDualizingSheaf π d ω` says that the `𝒪_X`-module `ω` is `H^{-d}(π^! k)`, where
`π^! = j^* ∘ π̄^×` for a compactification `X ⊆ X̄` of `π` (Stacks, Tag 0A9Y): `π̄^×` is the right
adjoint of `Rπ̄_*` (`Stacks.Duality.dualizingComplexOverField`, whose `H^{-d}` is
`Stacks.Duality.dualizingModuleOverField`). The downstream definitions take the Weil divisorial
subsheaf `ω_X(S) ⊆ K(X)` (`ωXS`) as an explicit argument; `DifferentHypotheses` ties it to an
embedding `ω ⊆ K(X)` of the dualizing sheaf by `ω_X(S) = ω · 𝒪_X(S)`.

## Main definitions

* `MMP.Flips.IsDualizingSheaf`: `ω_X = H^{-d}(π^! k)` (FA 16.3.3).
* `MMP.Flips.IsRegularAlong`, `MMP.Flips.restrictAlong`: `f` regular along `S` and `f|_S`
  (FA 16.3.6).
* `MMP.Flips.saturatedRestriction`: `i^{[*]}𝓕` (FA p. 174).
* `MMP.Flips.embeddedDualizingSheaf`: `Ω_S ⊆ K(S)` (FA 16.5).
* `MMP.Flips.weilRestrictionCartier`: `i^w_C 𝓛` (FA 16.3.6).
* `MMP.Flips.IsWeilRestriction`, `MMP.Flips.IsWeilRestrictionQ`: `i^w 𝓛` and `i^w B` (FA 16.3.6,
  16.5).
* `MMP.Flips.IsDifferentZero`, `MMP.Flips.IsDifferent`: `𝒟iff_S(0)` and `𝒟iff_S(B)` (FA 16.5).
* `MMP.Flips.IsDifferentDivisor`: `Diff_S(B)` (FA 16.6), under the hypotheses
  `MMP.Flips.DifferentHypotheses`.

## Implementation notes

* `restrictAlong` picks a preimage in `𝒪_{X,ξ}` of the germ `f_ξ ∈ K(X)_ξ`; the preimage, hence
  `f|_S`, is unique when `𝒪_{X,ξ} → K(X)_ξ` is injective (e.g. `X` reduced, as in FA). The value
  is the image in `𝒪_{S,ξ}`, which is the residue field `k(ξ)` when `S` is reduced.
* `embeddedDualizingSheaf` is defined as the saturation in `K(S)` of the image of
  `ε : i^*ω_X(S) → K(S)`, the `𝒪_S`-submodule generated by the restrictions `l|_S`. FA defines
  `Ω_S = ε_K(i^{[*]}ω_X(S))`; the two agree because `ε_K : 𝒢 ⊗ K(S) → K(S)` is injective (the
  first step of the proof of FA 16.5, `lem_fa16a_embedded_dualizing_sheaf_divisorial`), so that
  `ε_K` carries the saturation of `𝒢` to the saturation of `ε(𝒢)`. The morphisms `ε`, `ε_K` of
  sheaves of modules themselves are not constructed here.

## References

* [J. Kollár et al., *Flips and abundance for algebraic threefolds*][KollarFlips], 16.3.3,
  16.3.6, 16.5, 16.6
* [R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic geometry*][Har77], III.7
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9Y)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite Limits

namespace MMP.Flips

open MMP.Mori

/-! ### The dualizing sheaf -/

section Dualizing

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- `ω` is the *dualizing sheaf* of `X` (FA 16.3.3; Hartshorne III.7): `X`, with structure map
`π : X ⟶ Spec k`, is of pure dimension `d` (every irreducible component has dimension `d`), and
`ω ≅ ω_X = H^{-d}(ω_X^•)` for the normalized dualizing complex `ω_X^• = π^! k`.

Here `π^! = j^* ∘ π̄^×` for a compactification of `π`: an open immersion `j : X ⟶ X̄` and a proper
`π̄ : X̄ ⟶ Spec k` with `j ≫ π̄ = π` (Stacks, Tag 0A9Y), where `π̄^×(𝒪_{Spec k})` is
`Stacks.Duality.dualizingComplexOverField π̄`, the right adjoint of `Rπ̄_*` applied to `k`. Its
cohomology sheaf `H^{-d}` is `Stacks.Duality.dualizingModuleOverField π̄ d`, and
`H^{-d}(j^* K) = j^* H^{-d}(K)` because the restriction `j^*` to an open subscheme is exact; so
`ω_X = j^* H^{-d}(π̄^× k)`. The existence of a compactification (Nagata) and the independence of
the choice (Stacks, Tag 0ATX) are theorems, not part of the definition. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_dualizing_sheaf"]
def IsDualizingSheaf (π : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (d : ℕ) (ω : X.Modules) : Prop :=
  (∀ Z ∈ irreducibleComponents X, topologicalKrullDim Z = d) ∧
  ∃ (Xbar : Scheme.{u}) (j : X ⟶ Xbar) (_ : IsOpenImmersion j) (πbar : Xbar ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    (_ : IsProper πbar), j ≫ πbar = π ∧
    Nonempty (ω ≅ (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor j).obj
      (Stacks.Duality.dualizingModuleOverField πbar d))

end Dualizing

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (i : S ⟶ X)

/-! ### Generic points of a closed subscheme -/

/-- The closed subset `i(S) ⊆ X` of a closed immersion `i : S ⟶ X`. -/
def closedRange [IsClosedImmersion i] : Closeds X :=
  ⟨Set.range i.base, i.isClosedEmbedding.isClosed_range⟩

/-- A subset whose image under an inducing map is irreducible is irreducible. -/
theorem isIrreducible_of_isInducing_image {α β : Type*} [TopologicalSpace α]
    [TopologicalSpace β] {e : α → β} (he : Topology.IsInducing e) {A : Set α}
    (h : IsIrreducible (e '' A)) : IsIrreducible A := by
  refine ⟨Set.image_nonempty.mp h.nonempty, ?_⟩
  rintro u v hu hv ⟨x, hxA, hxu⟩ ⟨y, hyA, hyv⟩
  obtain ⟨u', hu', rfl⟩ := he.isOpen_iff.mp hu
  obtain ⟨v', hv', rfl⟩ := he.isOpen_iff.mp hv
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨z, hzA, rfl⟩, hzu, hzv⟩ :=
    h.2 u' v' hu' hv' ⟨e x, ⟨x, hxA, rfl⟩, hxu⟩ ⟨e y, ⟨y, hyA, rfl⟩, hyv⟩
  exact ⟨z, hzA, hzu, hzv⟩

/-- The image `i(η_Z)` of the generic point of an irreducible component `Z` of `S` is the generic
point of an irreducible component of the closed subset `i(S) ⊆ X`: its closure is a maximal
irreducible subset of `i(S)`. -/
theorem maximal_closure_image_genericPoint [IsClosedImmersion i] (Z : irreducibleComponents S) :
    Maximal (fun T : Set X => T ⊆ closedRange i ∧ IsIrreducible T)
      (closure {i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)}) := by
  have he := i.isClosedEmbedding
  have hcl : closure {i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)} = i.base '' Z.1 := by
    rw [← Set.image_singleton, he.isClosedMap.closure_image_eq_of_continuous he.continuous,
      (isGenericPoint_componentGenericPoint S Z).def]
  rw [hcl]
  refine ⟨⟨Set.image_subset_range _ _, Z.2.1.image _ he.continuous.continuousOn⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro T ⟨hTS, hT⟩ hZT
  have hpre : IsIrreducible (i.base ⁻¹' T) := by
    have : i.base '' (i.base ⁻¹' T) = T := Set.image_preimage_eq_of_subset hTS
    rw [← this] at hT
    exact isIrreducible_of_isInducing_image he.isInducing hT
  have hle : Z.1 ⊆ i.base ⁻¹' T := fun x hx => hZT ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  have := Z.2.2 hpre hle
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hTS hy
  exact ⟨x, this hy, rfl⟩

/-! ### Restriction of rational functions regular along `S` -/

/-- A section `f ∈ K(X)(V)` is *regular along `S`* (FA 16.3.6) if `f_ξ ∈ 𝒪_{X,ξ}` for every
generic point `ξ = i(η_Z)` of an irreducible component `Z` of `S` lying in `V`: the germ
`f_ξ ∈ K(X)_ξ` is in the image of `𝒪_{X,ξ} → K(X)_ξ`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_restriction_rational_functions"]
def IsRegularAlong {V : X.Opens} (f : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op V))) :
    Prop :=
  ∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents S) (h : i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z) ∈ V),
    (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).germ V _ h f ∈
      Set.range
        (structureStalkToRationalFunctionsStalk X (i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z))).hom

/-- The *restriction* `f|_S ∈ K(S)(S ∩ V)` of a section `f ∈ K(X)(V)` regular along `S`
(FA 16.3.6): `S ∩ V = i⁻¹(V)`, and the component of `f|_S` at the generic point `η_Z ∈ i⁻¹(V)` of
an irreducible component `Z` of `S` (where `K(S)_{η_Z} = 𝒪_{S,η_Z}`, which is `k(η_Z)` for `S`
reduced) is the image of `f_ξ ∈ 𝒪_{X,ξ}`, `ξ = i(η_Z)`, under `𝒪_{X,ξ} → 𝒪_{S,η_Z}`: the residue
class of `f_ξ`. The preimage of `f_ξ` in `𝒪_{X,ξ}` is chosen; it is unique when
`𝒪_{X,ξ} → K(X)_ξ` is injective (for instance for `X` reduced). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_restriction_rational_functions"]
def restrictAlong {V : X.Opens} (f : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op V)))
    (hf : IsRegularAlong i f) : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ V))) :=
  fun Z => (i.stalkMap (componentGenericPoint S Z.1)).hom (Classical.choose (hf Z.1 Z.2))

/-- The germs of `𝒪_X ⊆ K(X)` lie in the image of `𝒪_{X,x} → K(X)_x`. -/
theorem RationalFunctionsSubmodule.unit_stalkSet_subset (x : X) :
    (RationalFunctionsSubmodule.unit X).stalkSet x ⊆
      Set.range (structureStalkToRationalFunctionsStalk X x).hom := by
  rintro _ ⟨V, hV, s, hs, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨W, j, hxW, h⟩ := hs x hV
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Submodule.mem_one.mp h
  refine ⟨X.presheaf.germ W x hxW r, ?_⟩
  rw [← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply _ j x hxW, ← hr, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one,
    germ_smul_rationalFunctions, map_one, mul_one]

variable {i} in
/-- FA 16.5 and 16.3.6, "`l` is regular along `S` because `ω_X(S)_ξ = 𝒪_{X,ξ}` at the generic
points `ξ` of `S`": if `S` has pure codimension one in `X` (each `ξ` has codimension `≤ 1`) and
`𝓛 ∈ WSh_S(X)`, then every section of `𝓛` is regular along `S`. By (ii) of good support,
`𝓛_ξ = sat(𝒪_X)_ξ = 𝒪_{X,ξ}`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_embedded_dualizing_sheaf"]
theorem isRegularAlong_of_mem [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (hS : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents S, Order.coheight (i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)) ≤ 1)
    {L : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X} (hL : L ∈ goodSupportSubsheaves (closedRange i))
    {V : X.Opens} {l : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op V))}
    (hl : l ∈ L.sections V) : IsRegularAlong i l := by
  intro Z h
  have hmem : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).germ V _ h l ∈ L.stalkSet _ := ⟨V, h, l, hl, rfl⟩
  have hsupp := hL.2 _ (maximal_closure_image_genericPoint i Z)
  simp only [WeilDivisorialSubsheaf.support, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, not_not] at hsupp
  rw [hsupp, ← RationalFunctionsSubmodule.mem_stalk,
    RationalFunctionsSubmodule.stalk_saturation _ (hS Z),
    RationalFunctionsSubmodule.mem_stalk] at hmem
  exact RationalFunctionsSubmodule.unit_stalkSet_subset _ hmem

/-! ### The saturated restriction `i^{[*]}` -/

section SaturatedRestriction

/-- The sheaves of modules on a scheme with the sheafified tensor product of [Stacks, Tag 01CA]
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.OnSpace.monoidal`, with unit `𝒪_X`). -/
local instance modulesMonoidal (Y : Scheme.{u}) : MonoidalCategory Y.Modules :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.OnSpace.monoidal Y.toRingedSpace

variable (S) in
/-- `K(S)` as an `𝒪_S`-submodule of itself. -/
def RationalFunctionsSubmodule.top : RationalFunctionsSubmodule S where
  sections _ := ⊤
  map_mem _ := fun _ => Submodule.mem_top
  mem_of_locally _ := Submodule.mem_top

variable (S) in
/-- The sheaf of rational functions `K(S)` as an `𝒪_S`-module. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_saturated_restriction"]
def rationalFunctionsModule : S.Modules := (RationalFunctionsSubmodule.top S).toModules

variable (S) in
/-- The inclusion `𝒪_S ⟶ K(S)`, the morphism of `𝒪_S`-modules sending `1` to `1`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_saturated_restriction"]
def oneToRationalFunctions : 𝟙_ S.Modules ⟶ rationalFunctionsModule S :=
  (rationalFunctionsModule S).unitHomEquiv.symm
    ⟨fun U => (⟨1, Submodule.mem_top⟩ : (RationalFunctionsSubmodule.top S).sections U.unop), by
      intro U V j
      exact Subtype.ext (map_one ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).map j).hom)⟩

/-- The canonical map `𝒢 → 𝒢 ⊗_{𝒪_S} K(S)`, `g ↦ g ⊗ 1`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_saturated_restriction"]
def toTensorRationalFunctions (G : S.Modules) : G ⟶ G ⊗ rationalFunctionsModule S :=
  (ρ_ G).inv ≫ (G ◁ oneToRationalFunctions S)

/-- `𝒢 = i^*𝓕 / Tors_{𝒪_S}(i^*𝓕)` (FA p. 174), where `i^*𝓕 = 𝓕 ⊗_{𝒪_X} 𝒪_S` is the pullback
and `Tors` is the kernel of `i^*𝓕 → i^*𝓕 ⊗_{𝒪_S} K(S)`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_saturated_restriction"]
def torsionFreeRestriction (F : X.Modules) : S.Modules :=
  cokernel (kernel.ι (toTensorRationalFunctions ((Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj F)))

/-- The *saturated restriction* `i^{[*]}𝓕` (FA p. 174): the saturation, inside
`𝒢 ⊗_{𝒪_S} K(S)`, of `𝒢 = i^*𝓕 / Tors` (`torsionFreeRestriction`). Its sections over `V` are the
sections `t` of `𝒢 ⊗ K(S)` over `V` whose germs at the points `P ∈ V` of codimension `≤ 1` of `S`
lie in `𝒢` (the image of `𝒢 → 𝒢 ⊗ K(S)`): near each such `P`, `t` is the image of a section of
`𝒢`. FA applies this to coherent `𝓕`; the definition needs no hypothesis. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_saturated_restriction"]
def saturatedRestriction (F : X.Modules) (V : S.Opens) :
    Set (((torsionFreeRestriction i F) ⊗ rationalFunctionsModule S).val.obj (op V)) :=
  {t | ∀ P ∈ V, Order.coheight P ≤ 1 → ∃ (W : S.Opens) (j : W ⟶ V), P ∈ W ∧
    ∃ g : (torsionFreeRestriction i F).val.obj (op W),
      ((torsionFreeRestriction i F) ⊗ rationalFunctionsModule S).val.map j.op t =
        (toTensorRationalFunctions (torsionFreeRestriction i F)).val.app (op W) g}

end SaturatedRestriction

/-! ### The embedded dualizing sheaf `Ω_S` -/

/-- The restrictions `l|_S`, over an open `V ⊆ S`, of the sections `l ∈ 𝓛(W)` regular along `S`
over the opens `W ⊆ X` with `V ⊆ S ∩ W`: the values `ε(l ⊗ 1)` of `ε : i^*𝓛 → K(S)`,
`l ⊗ s ↦ (l|_S) s`, on the pure tensors with `s = 1`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_embedded_dualizing_sheaf"]
def restrictionSet (L : RationalFunctionsSubmodule X) (V : S.Opens) :
    Set (ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).obj (op V))) :=
  {g | ∃ (W : X.Opens) (h : V ≤ i ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (l : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op W))) (_ : l ∈ L.sections W)
    (hl : IsRegularAlong i l),
    g = (rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).map (homOfLE h).op (restrictAlong i l hl)}

/-- The restriction along `V' ⟶ V` of an element of `restrictionSet i L V` lies in
`restrictionSet i L V'`. -/
theorem restrictionSet_map (L : RationalFunctionsSubmodule X) {V V' : S.Opens} (j : V' ⟶ V)
    {g : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).obj (op V))} (hg : g ∈ restrictionSet i L V) :
    (rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).map j.op g ∈ restrictionSet i L V' := by
  obtain ⟨W, h, l, hlL, hl, rfl⟩ := hg
  exact ⟨W, j.le.trans h, l, hlL, hl, rationalFunctionsPresheaf_map_map _ _ _ _⟩

/-- The image `ε(i^*𝓛) ⊆ K(S)` of `ε : i^*𝓛 → K(S)`, `l ⊗ s ↦ (l|_S) s`: the subsheaf of `K(S)`
generated by the `𝒪_S`-submodules spanned by the restrictions `l|_S` (`restrictionSet`). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_embedded_dualizing_sheaf"]
def restrictionImage (L : RationalFunctionsSubmodule X) : RationalFunctionsSubmodule S :=
  RationalFunctionsSubmodule.localClosure
    (fun V => Submodule.span Γ(S, V) (restrictionSet i L V)) fun {U V} j s hs => by
      induction hs using Submodule.span_induction with
      | mem x hx => exact Submodule.subset_span (restrictionSet_map i L j hx)
      | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
      | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hx hy
      | smul r x _ hx =>
        rw [rationalFunctionsPresheaf_map_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hx

/-- The embedded dualizing sheaf `Ω_S ⊆ K(S)` (FA 16.5) of `S`, for the Weil divisorial subsheaf
`ωXS = ω_X(S) ∈ WSh_S(X)`: FA defines it as `ε_K(i^{[*]}ω_X(S))`, the image of the saturated
restriction (`saturatedRestriction`) under the `K(S)`-linear extension
`ε_K : 𝒢 ⊗ K(S) → K(S)` of `ε : ω_X(S) ⊗ 𝒪_S → K(S)`, `l ⊗ s ↦ (l|_S) s`
(`l` is regular along `S` by `isRegularAlong_of_mem`).

Here it is the saturation in `K(S)` of the image `ε(i^*ω_X(S))` (`restrictionImage`): its
sections over `V` are the `s ∈ K(S)(V)` whose germ at every point `P ∈ V` of codimension `≤ 1`
of `S` lies in the `𝒪_{S,P}`-span of the restrictions `(l|_S)_P`, `l ∈ ω_X(S)_{i(P)}`. This is
`ε_K(i^{[*]}ω_X(S))` because `ε_K` is injective (proof of FA 16.5), so it carries the saturation
of `𝒢` in `𝒢 ⊗ K(S)` onto the saturation of `ε(𝒢) = ε(i^*ω_X(S))` in `K(S)`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_embedded_dualizing_sheaf"]
def embeddedDualizingSheaf (ωXS : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X) : RationalFunctionsSubmodule S :=
  (restrictionImage i ωXS.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule).saturation

/-! ### The restriction `i^w` -/

/-- The condition on a germ `g ∈ K(S)_P` defining `i^w_C 𝓛` (FA 16.3.6): if `P` has codimension
`≤ 1` in `S`, then for every generator `f` of the free `𝒪_{X,P}`-module `𝓛_P`
(`𝓛_P = f · 𝒪_{X,P}` with `f` a unit of `K(X)_P`, as in `IsInvertibleAt`), `g ∈ (f|_S)_P 𝒪_{S,P}`.
Here `(f|_S)_P` is the germ at `P` of `f'|_S` for any section `f'` of `K(X)` over a
neighbourhood `W` of `P` with germ `f` and regular along `S`; it does not depend on `f'`, and such
an `f'` exists (`exists_isRegularAlong_germ_eq`). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_weil_restriction_cartier"]
def WeilRestrictionCartierCondition (L : RationalFunctionsSubmodule X) (P : S)
    (g : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).stalk P) : Prop :=
  Order.coheight P ≤ 1 →
    ∀ f : ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).stalk (i.base P))ˣ,
      L.stalkSet (i.base P) = Set.range (fun a : X.presheaf.stalk (i.base P) =>
        (f : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).stalk (i.base P)) *
          (structureStalkToRationalFunctionsStalk X (i.base P)).hom a) →
      ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hP : i.base P ∈ W)
        (f' : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op W))) (hf' : IsRegularAlong i f'),
        (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).germ W _ hP f' = f →
        ∃ a : S.presheaf.stalk P, g =
          (rationalFunctionsPresheaf S).germ (i ⁻¹ᵁ W) P hP (restrictAlong i f' hf') *
            (structureStalkToRationalFunctionsStalk S P).hom a

/-- `i^w_C 𝓛 ⊆ K(S)` (FA 16.3.6), for `𝓛 ∈ WSh_S(X)` invertible at every point of `S` of
codimension `≤ 1` in `S`: the subsheaf whose sections over an open `V ⊆ S` are the
`s ∈ K(S)(V)` such that for every `P ∈ V` of codimension `≤ 1` in `S` and every generator `f` of
the free `𝒪_{X,P}`-module `𝓛_P`, `s_P ∈ (f|_S)_P 𝒪_{S,P}` (`WeilRestrictionCartierCondition`).
The construction makes sense for every `𝒪_X`-submodule `𝓛 ⊆ K(X)`; it is used (in
`IsWeilRestriction`) only under FA's hypotheses. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_weil_restriction_cartier"]
def weilRestrictionCartier (L : RationalFunctionsSubmodule X) : RationalFunctionsSubmodule S :=
  RationalFunctionsSubmodule.ofStalkCondition (WeilRestrictionCartierCondition i L)
    (fun P _ f _ W hP f' hf' _ => ⟨0, by rw [map_zero, mul_zero]⟩)
    (fun P a b ha hb hc f hf W hP f' hf' hg => by
      obtain ⟨a', ha'⟩ := ha hc f hf W hP f' hf' hg
      obtain ⟨b', hb'⟩ := hb hc f hf W hP f' hf' hg
      exact ⟨a' + b', by rw [map_add, mul_add, ha', hb']⟩)
    (fun P r a ha hc f hf W hP f' hf' hg => by
      obtain ⟨a', ha'⟩ := ha hc f hf W hP f' hf' hg
      exact ⟨r * a', by rw [ha', map_mul]; ring⟩)

variable {i} in
/-- FA 16.3.6, "every such `f` is regular along `S` near `P`, as `𝓛_ξ = 𝒪_{X,ξ}` at the generic
points `ξ` of `S` by (ii) of good support": for `𝓛 ∈ WSh_S(X)`, `S` of pure codimension one, and
a generator `f` of `𝓛_P`, there are a neighbourhood `W` of `P` and a section `f'` of `K(X)` over
`W`, regular along `S`, with germ `f` at `P`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_weil_restriction_cartier"]
theorem exists_isRegularAlong_germ_eq [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (hS : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents S, Order.coheight (i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)) ≤ 1)
    {L : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X} (hL : L ∈ goodSupportSubsheaves (closedRange i)) (P : S)
    (f : ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).stalk (i.base P))ˣ)
    (hf : L.stalkSet (i.base P) = Set.range (fun a : X.presheaf.stalk (i.base P) =>
        (f : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).stalk (i.base P)) *
          (structureStalkToRationalFunctionsStalk X (i.base P)).hom a)) :
    ∃ (W : X.Opens) (hP : i.base P ∈ W)
      (f' : ToType ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op W))) (_ : IsRegularAlong i f'),
      (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).germ W _ hP f' = f := by
  have hmem : (f : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).stalk (i.base P)) ∈ L.stalkSet (i.base P) := by
    rw [hf]; exact ⟨1, by simp⟩
  obtain ⟨W, hP, f', hf'L, hgerm⟩ := hmem
  exact ⟨W, hP, f', isRegularAlong_of_mem hS hL hf'L, hgerm⟩

/-- `M ∈ WSh(S)_ℚ` is *the restriction* `i^w 𝓛 = 𝓛|S` of `𝓛 ∈ WSh_S(X)` (FA 16.3.6) if
`M = (1/n) i^w_C(𝓛^[n])` for some `n ≥ 1` such that `𝓛^[n]` is invertible at every point of `S`
of codimension `≤ 1` in `S`. The class `(1/n) i^w_C(𝓛^[n])` is formed from a Weil divisorial
subsheaf `𝓝` of `S` equal to `i^w_C(𝓛^[n])` (that it is one is
`lem_fa16a_weil_restriction_cartier_divisorial`). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_weil_restriction"]
def IsWeilRestriction [IsClosedImmersion i] (L : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X)
    (M : QWeilDivisorialSheaf S) : Prop :=
  L ∈ goodSupportSubsheaves (closedRange i) ∧
    ∃ n : ℕ+, (∀ P : S, Order.coheight P ≤ 1 →
      (L.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule.reflexivePow (n : ℕ)).IsInvertibleAt (i.base P)) ∧
      ∃ N : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf S, N.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule =
          weilRestrictionCartier i (L.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule.reflexivePow (n : ℕ)) ∧
        M = N.divNat n

/-- `R ∈ WSh(S)_ℚ` is `i^w B` for `B ∈ WSh_S(X)_ℚ` (FA 16.5): for `B = (1/m)𝓛` with
`𝓛 ∈ WSh_S(X)`, `i^w B = (1/m) i^w 𝓛`. With `i^w 𝓛 = (1/n)𝓝` (`IsWeilRestriction`),
`(1/m)·(1/n)𝓝 = (1/mn)𝓝`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_weil_restriction_q"]
def IsWeilRestrictionQ [IsClosedImmersion i] (B : QWeilDivisorialSheaf X)
    (R : QWeilDivisorialSheaf S) : Prop :=
  ∃ (L : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X) (m : ℕ+), L ∈ goodSupportSubsheaves (closedRange i) ∧
    B = L.divNat m ∧ ∃ (N : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf S) (n : ℕ+),
      IsWeilRestriction i L (N.divNat n) ∧ R = N.divNat (m * n)

/-! ### The differents -/

namespace QWeilDivisorialSheaf

/-- The identity `c₁ + c₂ = c₃` in `WSh(Y)_ℚ`, written additively (the book writes
`c₁ · c₂ = c₃`), on representatives: `cᵢ = (1/nᵢ)𝓛ᵢ` and
`(1/n₁)𝓛₁ + (1/n₂)𝓛₂ = (1/n₁n₂)(𝓛₁^[n₂] · 𝓛₂^[n₁])` (FA 16.1.2, 16.1.3), whose equality with
`(1/n₃)𝓛₃` is the relation of FA 16.1.3: `(𝓛₁^[n₂] · 𝓛₂^[n₁])^[m n₃] = 𝓛₃^[m n₁ n₂]` for some
`m ≥ 1`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_different_zero"]
def IsSum {Y : Scheme.{u}} (c₁ c₂ c₃ : QWeilDivisorialSheaf Y) : Prop :=
  ∃ (L₁ L₂ L₃ : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf Y) (n₁ n₂ n₃ : ℕ+),
    c₁ = L₁.divNat n₁ ∧ c₂ = L₂.divNat n₂ ∧ c₃ = L₃.divNat n₃ ∧
    ∃ m : ℕ, 1 ≤ m ∧
      ((L₁.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule.reflexivePow (n₂ : ℕ)).mul
          (L₂.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule.reflexivePow (n₁ : ℕ))).reflexivePow
            (m * n₃ : ℕ) =
        L₃.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule.reflexivePow (m * (n₁ * n₂) : ℕ)

end QWeilDivisorialSheaf

/-- `D ∈ WSh(S)_ℚ` is *the different* `𝒟iff_S(0)` of `S ⊆ X` (FA Prop.–Def. 16.5), for the fixed
embedding giving `ωXS = ω_X(S) ∈ WSh_S(X)`, if `[Ω_S] + D = M` where `M = i^w ω_X(S)`
(`IsWeilRestriction`) and `[Ω_S] = (1/1)Ω_S` is the class of the embedded dualizing sheaf
(`embeddedDualizingSheaf`, a Weil divisorial subsheaf of `S` by FA 16.5). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_different_zero"]
def IsDifferentZero [IsClosedImmersion i] (ωXS : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X)
    (D : QWeilDivisorialSheaf S) : Prop :=
  ∃ (Ω : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf S) (M : QWeilDivisorialSheaf S),
    Ω.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule = embeddedDualizingSheaf i ωXS ∧
      IsWeilRestriction i ωXS M ∧ QWeilDivisorialSheaf.IsSum (Ω.divNat 1) D M

/-- For `B ∈ WSh_S(X)_ℚ`, `D' ∈ WSh(S)_ℚ` is *the different* `𝒟iff_S(B)` of `B`
(FA Prop.–Def. 16.5) if `D' = D + i^w B` with `D = 𝒟iff_S(0)` (`IsDifferentZero`) and `i^w B` as
in `IsWeilRestrictionQ` (the book writes `𝒟iff(B) = 𝒟iff(0) · i^w B`). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_different"]
def IsDifferent [IsClosedImmersion i] (ωXS : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X)
    (B : QWeilDivisorialSheaf X) (D' : QWeilDivisorialSheaf S) : Prop :=
  B ∈ goodSupportQSheaves (closedRange i) ∧
    ∃ D R : QWeilDivisorialSheaf S, IsDifferentZero i ωXS D ∧ IsWeilRestrictionQ i B R ∧
      QWeilDivisorialSheaf.IsSum D R D'

/-- `c ∈ WSh(Y)_ℚ` is the class of the `ℚ`-Weil divisor `B` (FA 16.2.2): `c = (1/m)𝒪_Y(E)` for
some `m ≥ 1` and `E ∈ WDiv(Y)` with `mB = E`, the subsheaf `𝒪_Y(E) ⊆ K(Y)` being a Weil
divisorial subsheaf. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_different_divisor"]
def IsQSheafOfQWeilDivisor {Y : Scheme.{u}} (B : QWeilDivisor Y) (c : QWeilDivisorialSheaf Y) :
    Prop :=
  ∃ (m : ℕ+) (E : WeilDivisor Y) (N : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf Y),
    (∀ Γ, (m : ℚ) * B Γ = E Γ) ∧ N.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule = E.sheaf ∧ c = N.divNat m

open scoped Classical in
/-- The hypotheses `(⋆)` of FA 16.6, without "`K_X + S + B` is lc in codimension two": `X` is a
normal variety over `k` with structure map `π`; `i : S ⟶ X` is a reduced closed subscheme of pure
codimension one; `DS` is the reduced Weil divisor `S` (coefficient `1` at the generic points of
the components of `S`, which are prime divisors along which `X` is a DVR); `B = ∑ bᵢ Bᵢ` is a
`ℚ`-Weil divisor whose prime divisors are not contained in `S`, with `0 ≤ bᵢ ≤ 1`; `ω ⊆ K(X)` is
an embedding of the dualizing sheaf `ω_X` (`IsDualizingSheaf`) such that
`ωXS = ω_X(S) = ω_X · 𝒪_X(S)` lies in `WSh_S(X)`. -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_different_divisor"]
structure DifferentHypotheses {k : Type u} [Field k] (π : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (d : ℕ)
    [IsClosedImmersion i] (ω ωXS : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X) (DS : WeilDivisor X)
    (B : QWeilDivisor X) : Prop where
  /-- `X` is a normal variety. -/
  isNormalVariety : IsNormalVariety k π
  /-- `S` is reduced. -/
  isReduced : IsReduced S
  /-- `S` has pure codimension one in `X`. -/
  coheight_eq_one : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents S,
    Order.coheight (i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)) = 1
  /-- The components of `S` are prime divisors along which `X` is a DVR. -/
  exists_weilDivisorPrime : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents S,
    ∃ Γ : WeilDivisorPrime X, Γ.1.genericPoint = i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)
  /-- `DS` is the reduced divisor `S`. -/
  coeff_divisor : ∀ Γ : WeilDivisorPrime X, DS Γ =
    if ∃ Z : irreducibleComponents S, Γ.1.genericPoint = i.base (componentGenericPoint S Z)
    then 1 else 0
  /-- The coefficients of `B` are `≥ 0`. -/
  coeff_nonneg : ∀ Γ, 0 ≤ B Γ
  /-- The coefficients of `B` are `≤ 1`. -/
  coeff_le_one : ∀ Γ, B Γ ≤ 1
  /-- The prime divisors of `B` are not contained in `S`. -/
  not_subset : ∀ Γ, B Γ ≠ 0 → Γ.1.genericPoint ∉ Set.range i.base
  /-- `ω ⊆ K(X)` is an embedding of the dualizing sheaf. -/
  isDualizingSheaf : IsDualizingSheaf π d ω.toModules
  /-- `ω_X(S) = ω_X · 𝒪_X(S)`. -/
  twist_eq : ωXS.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule = ω.twist DS
  /-- `ω_X(S) ∈ WSh_S(X)`. -/
  mem_goodSupportSubsheaves : ωXS ∈ goodSupportSubsheaves (closedRange i)

/-- Under the hypotheses `(⋆)` (`DifferentHypotheses`), a `ℚ`-Weil divisor
`Δ = (1/n)D ∈ WDiv(S)_ℚ` (`D ∈ WDiv(S)`, `n ≥ 1`) is *the different* `Diff_S(B)` (FA Prop. 16.6)
if `(1/n)𝒪_S(D)` is the different `𝒟iff_S(B)` (`IsDifferent`) of the class of `B` in
`WSh_S(X)_ℚ` (`IsQSheafOfQWeilDivisor`). -/
@[mmp "def_fa16a_different_divisor"]
def IsDifferentDivisor {k : Type u} [Field k] (π : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (d : ℕ)
    [IsClosedImmersion i] (ω ωXS : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf X) (DS : WeilDivisor X)
    (B : QWeilDivisor X) (Δ : QWeilDivisor S) : Prop :=
  DifferentHypotheses i π d ω ωXS DS B ∧
    ∃ (c : QWeilDivisorialSheaf X), IsQSheafOfQWeilDivisor B c ∧
      ∃ (n : ℕ+) (D : WeilDivisor S) (N : WeilDivisorialSubsheaf S),
        (∀ Γ, Δ Γ = (D Γ : ℚ) / n) ∧ N.toRationalFunctionsSubmodule = D.sheaf ∧
          IsDifferent i ωXS c (N.divNat n)

end MMP.Flips
